  "text": "### 6. Capital Risk  \n**Appetite:** Conservative  \n**Tolerance:**\n- **Capital Ratio (Pillar 1):** >15% minimum, 18%+ target\n- **Leverage Ratio:** >5% (per Basel III)\n- **Dividend Policy:** Conservative (retain earnings for growth)\n- **Capital Adequacy Buffer:** 3%+ above minimum  \n**Rationale:**\nFirstUK Bank maintains strong capital ratios to absorb losses, fund growth, and meet regulatory requirements. Does not maximize shareholder returns at expense of stability.  \n**Controls:**\n- Annual capital planning\n- Stress testing (multiple scenarios)\n- Capital forecasting\n- Dividend policy (Board-approved)\n- Regular ratio monitoring  \n---",
